ntation based on Difference-Bound Matrices—O(n2) memory cost, where n is the number of variables—and graph-based algorithms for all common abstract operators—O(n3) time cost. This includes a normal form algorithm to test equivalence of representation and a widening operator to compute least fixpoint approximations.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"This article presents a new numerical abstract domain for static analysis by abstract interpretation. It extends a former numerical abstract domain based on Difference-Bound Matrices and allows us to represent invariants of the form (±x ± y ≤ c), where x and y are program variables and c is a real constant.\r\nWe focus on giving an efficient representation based on Difference-Bound Matrices—O(n2) memory cost, where n is the number of variables—and graph-based algorithms for all common abstract operators—O(n3) time cost. This includes a normal form algorithm to test equivalence of representation and a widening operator to compute least fixpoint approximations.","submitter_user":"dbremner","user_is_author":false,"tags":["compilers","pdf","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/trppty","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/trppty/octagon_abstract_domain_2007"},{"short_id":"mkfn1p","created_at":"2021-07-07T12:47:26.000-05:00","title":"Visibility Buffer Rendering with Material Graphs","url":"http://filmicworlds.com/blog/visibility-buffer-rendering-with-material-graphs/","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"friendlysock","user_is_author":false,"tags":["graphics"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/mkfn1p","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/mkfn1p/visibility_buffer_rendering_with"},{"short_id":"jnstq9","created_at":"2021-07-07T12:24:02.000-05:00","title":"A Comparison of Ruby Version Managers for macOS","url":"https://www.sitepoint.com/ruby-version-managers-macos/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":4,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_use